<title>GERMANY: Fresenius buys French medical products firm.</title>
<headline>Fresenius buys French medical products firm.</headline>
<dateline>BAD HOMBURG, Germany 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German medical equipment manufacturer Fresenius AG said on Tuesday it had bought French company Vial Medical Infusion Systems S.A. from Becton Dickinson France S.A.</p>
<p>Vial Medical Infusion Systems is based in Brezins, France, employs about 120 people and generated sales of about 38 million marks in its 1995/96 business year, Fresenius said in a mandatory statement.</p>
<p>The statement did not disclose the purchase price.</p>
<p>Fresenius said it had bought Vial on October 28 to strengthen its activities in the area of infusion technology.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
